<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Ryan Hotels half-yr pre-tax profit up 31pct.</title>
<headline>Ryan Hotels half-yr pre-tax profit up 31pct.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>26 weeks to July, 1996</p>
<p>					  (million punts unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		2.18		   vs 1.68</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 0.625		  vs 0.5</p>
<p> Pretax profit	    1.61		   vs 1.23</p>
<p> Turnover		   13.86		  vs 13.17</p>
<p> Trading profit	   2.70		   vs 2.40</p>
<p> Tax charge		 0.06		   vs 0.03</p>
<p> Net taxed		  1.55		   vs 1.20</p>
<p> Retained profit	  1.20		   vs 0.84</p>
<p> Record date	 15-10-96</p>
<p> Pay date	    22-11-96</p>
<p>Ex-dividend date  07-10-96</p>
<p>NOTE - Irish hotel group Ryan Hotels Plc said market conditions were strong both in Ireland and on the continent and it was looking forward to an excellent full year outturn.</p>
<p>-- Dublin newsroom 353 1 660 3377</p>
</text>
